capability admit-api-run-live
intent: Admit a run of a declared capability through the declared API and declare its whole plan: the run store of the sfx-identity database registers it under the caller session (an idempotencyKey in the admission names the same run for the same caller), and the answer is the host directive (sfx-api-host-directive.v1) the hosting facade carries out step by step, deciding none of it. execute-run carries the response the client receives, complete as declared (202 with the run; its body ends where the facade closes the connection, as its Connection: close says), and the run: its id, admission time and capability; its envelope, which asks the kernel for its observations (delivery-observation.v1: sample true, its stream named by the run id); the capability that shapes its events (project-api-run-events); its trace capability (append-api-run-trace); its completion capability (complete-api-run) with the completion input; its fact capture (capture-estate-live-observation-facts); and, for the run and for each of them, whether its execution is published to the estate live observation channel: the run's is, and none of the others is. A replayed key answers respond with the same 202 and executes nothing. A refused registration answers its refusal.
outcome: a host directive (application/vnd.sfx.host-directive+json, sfx-api-host-directive.v1): execute-run with the declared 202 response and the run's plan, or respond for a replayed key; a refused registration answers its refusal
inquiry: Which run did this admission create, and what is its plan?
input contract admit-api-run-live-request.v1 {"type":"object"}
output contract admit-api-run-live-result.v1 {"type":"object"}
cli display outcome as json
scenario admit-api-run-live root terminal
given: an admission (object, operation, subject, namespace, input, idempotencyKey) with the caller principal and session
when: the run store registers the run
then: the outcome is the host directive for the registered run
operation admit-api-run-live.register-prepare kind invoke-port port admit-api-run-live-register-prepare
operation admit-api-run-live.register kind invoke-port port admit-api-run-live-register
operation admit-api-run-live.answer kind invoke-port port admit-api-run-live-answer
platform bind admit-api-run-live-register-prepare
platform: sda-authority-transformation-port.v1
config: {"expression":{"op":"object","fields":{"executionTarget":{"op":"literal","value":"sql-database-reader"},"executionNamespace":{"op":"literal","value":"sidefx:capabilities"},"executionScenario":{"op":"literal","value":"sql-database-reader"},"inputType":{"op":"literal","value":"json"},"dispatchRequest":{"op":"object","fields":{"dataSource":{"op":"literal","value":"sfx-identity-database"},"statement":{"op":"literal","value":"SET NOCOUNT ON; DECLARE @principal_id uniqueidentifier = TRY_CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.principalId')); DECLARE @session_id uniqueidentifier = TRY_CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.sessionId')); DECLARE @object nvarchar(64) = COALESCE(JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.admission.object'), N'capability'); DECLARE @operation nvarchar(64) = COALESCE(JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.admission.operation'), N'observe'); DECLARE @capability_id nvarchar(512) = JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.admission.subject'); DECLARE @namespace_id nvarchar(256) = COALESCE(JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.admission.namespace'), N'sidefx:capabilities'); DECLARE @header_key nvarchar(4000) = NULLIF(JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.idempotencyKey'), N''); DECLARE @body_key nvarchar(4000) = NULLIF(JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.admission.idempotencyKey'), N''); IF @header_key IS NOT NULL AND @body_key IS NOT NULL AND @header_key <> @body_key THROW 51000, 'IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_CONFLICT', 1; DECLARE @key nvarchar(4000) = COALESCE(@header_key, @body_key); IF @object <> N'capability' OR @operation NOT IN (N'observe', N'invoke') OR @capability_id IS NULL OR LEN(@capability_id) = 0 THROW 51000, 'ADMISSION_INVALID', 1; IF @key IS NOT NULL AND (LEN(@key) = 0 OR LEN(@key) > 200) THROW 51000, 'IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_INVALID', 1; DECLARE @run_id varchar(128) = CASE WHEN @key IS NULL THEN LOWER(CONVERT(varchar(36), NEWID())) ELSE LOWER(CONVERT(varchar(36), CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, SUBSTRING(HASHBYTES('SHA2_256', CONCAT(N'sfx-api-admission:', CONVERT(nvarchar(36), @principal_id), N':', @key)), 1, 16)))) END; DECLARE @before datetime2(7) = SYSUTCDATETIME(); DECLARE @r TABLE(run_id varchar(128), admitted_at datetime2(7)); BEGIN TRY INSERT @r EXEC evidence.register_run @run_id = @run_id, @principal_id = @principal_id, @session_id = @session_id, @capability_id = @capability_id, @namespace_id = @namespace_id, @writer_id = 'sfx-api'; END TRY BEGIN CATCH IF ERROR_MESSAGE() = 'EVIDENCE_CONFLICT' AND @key IS NOT NULL THROW 51000, 'IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_CONFLICT', 1; THROW; END CATCH; SELECT (SELECT r.run_id AS runId, CONVERT(datetimeoffset(7), r.admitted_at) AS admittedAt, CONVERT(bit, CASE WHEN r.admitted_at < @before THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS replayed, @operation AS operation, @namespace_id AS namespace, JSON_QUERY(@input, '$.admission') AS admission FROM @r r FOR JSON PATH, WITHOUT_ARRAY_WRAPPER) AS value;"},"resultColumn":{"op":"literal","value":"value"},"input":{"op":"path","path":""}}}}}}
platform bind admit-api-run-live-register
